{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FovBi29kCmtH5khbdbG863","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd095-nohup\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/nohup: Run a Command Immune to Hangups\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships nohup but the GNU version has specific behavior for stdout/stderr\n6\t  redirection to nohup.out. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n7\t  binary (gnohup, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n8\t  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Run a command immune to SIGHUP, with stdout/stderr redirection when not a terminal.\n12\t  - G2: Verify functional parity against gnohup via differential testing.\n13\t\n14\trequirements:\n15\t  R1:\n16\t    title: SIGHUP immunity and output redirection\n17\t    items:\n18\t      - R1.1:\n19\t          text: Must ignore SIGHUP (signal.Ignore(syscall.SIGHUP)) before executing COMMAND.\n20\t      - R1.2:\n21\t          text: If stdout is a terminal, must redirect stdout to nohup.out in the current directory. If that fails, must redirect to $HOME/nohup.out. Must print a message to stderr indicating where output is redirected.\n22\t      - R1.3:\n23\t          text: If stderr is a terminal and stdout has been redirected, must redirect stderr to stdout (i.e., both go to nohup.out).\n24\t      - R1.4:\n25\t          text: Must pass all remaining arguments after COMMAND as arguments to the executed command.\n26\t\n27\t  R2:\n28\t    title: Exit codes\n29\t    items:\n30\t      - R2.1:\n31\t          text: Must exit with the exit status of COMMAND when COMMAND completes.\n32\t      - R2.2:\n33\t          text: Must exit 125 when nohup itself fails. Must exit 126 when COMMAND is found but cannot be invoked. Must exit 127 when COMMAND is not found.\n34\t      - R2.3:\n35\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n36\t\n37\tnon_goals:\n38\t  - cmd/nohup does not implement --help or --version beyond usage on error.\n39\t\n40\tacceptance_criteria:\n41\t  - id: AC1\n42\t    criterion: \"nohup echo hello redirects output to nohup.out when stdout is a terminal, matching gnohup.\"\n43\t    traces:\n44\t      - R1.1\n45\t      - R1.2\n46\t      - R1.4\n47\t  - id: AC2\n48\t    criterion: \"nohup missing-cmd exits 127, matching gnohup.\"\n49\t    traces:\n50\t      - R2.2\n51\t  - id: AC3\n52\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gnohup passes for all required test cases.\"\n53\t    traces:\n54\t      - R1.1\n55\t      - R1.2\n56\t      - R1.3\n57\t  - id: AC4\n58\t    criterion: \"cmd/nohup compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n59\t    traces:\n60\t      - R1.1\n61\t      - R1.2\n62\t      - R1.3\n63\t      - R1.4\n64\t      - R2.1\n65\t      - R2.2\n66\t      - R2.3\n67\t\n68\tpackage_contract:\n69\t  imports:\n70\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n71\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0192rDUJ6XJAgApvpPxqMxxn","session_id":"3a78f972-7946-4822-be55-ef36be9580af","uuid":"e399961d-0f9f-4b6a-a21a-2524c8e1c0d4","timestamp":"2026-05-24T03:12:45.899Z"}
